Subject: [PATCH] TEACH-LOCK (web): Teach shows golden VerifyMotorAction's lock
 -- labLock "*Lock by ... moveing", pnlStop yellow, MoveN / MoveP / Home /
 MoveTo disabled -- for the selected axis (same rule as Motor Test)

The every-component check found labLock and pnlStop never written on this page. Golden uteach.cpp:5346-5405 (every tick while
Teach or Motor Test is shown) -> LockAllButton :5321-5329 + labLock :5399-5404. C++ already computes it (runtime "lock",
WebMotorAccessLive.cpp:1271 / ChanMotorPoints.cpp:437-446, the block Motor Test draws); page/ht9045_teach_lock_c.js draws it from
the page's 1 s runtime poll.

Deviation, same as Motor Test (EastSun 20260929 MT-AXISLOCK): only the SELECTED axis locks; PageControl2 (every tab) is never
disabled. JOG is not locked (golden does not either). An old C++ without perAxis falls back to the whole-page button lock.

Verified: syntax OK; headless Edge with a runtime where MInArmX moves: labLock "*Lock by MInArmX moveing" shown, pnlStop
#ffff00, btnMoveN / btnHome disabled, btnJogP enabled; with the real idle snapshot nothing locks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
